{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqqmeewyhir","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"P4 finding (2026-06-23): after the P3 de-port, all LOCALLY-RUNNABLE benches that follow the probe/wiring/judge contract already route through the SDK (arms.run_canonical_wiring → POST /judge/drain) — so most \"migration\" was already done by P3. TWO genuine hand-rolled-judge HOLDOUTS remain, NOT yet on the SDK (neither blocks the bench-prod-parity feature): (1) scripts/bench-economy-dag.js — inline judgeEdge() claude -p KEEP/PRUNE rubric (~L271-282) + hard DAG_SCORE_THRESHOLD=0.5 fetchDagContext (~L284-312); migrate by subprocessing the Python SDK drain OR injecting raw top-K /search hits and deleting the 0.5 floor — do NOT keep the parallel JS rubric. (2) bench/swe-bench-cl/zonoid_memory.py — ZonoidMemorySystem._llm_judge (~L362) + _judge→POST /judge/verdict (~L524-530); a requests-based EXTERNAL-notebook adapter for the Mac/Docker SWE-bench pilot (not locally runnable); rewrite retrieve_relevant_experience to mint a probe + client.judge_drain, delete _llm_judge/_judge, switch requests→stdlib ZonoidClient — DEFER until that external pilot actually runs. These were emitted as P4 holdouts but the complete() follow_ups array was REFUSED by the daemon (it gates follow_ups to status:done, but the worker handoff mandates status:tested) — a small orchestrator inconsistency worth fixing; captured here so the work isn't lost.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T12:31:36.844Z"}
